[h1]Server Guide[/h1]

author=leozimmelo
[b]Publish your server's guides and rules, read in-game in a clean windowed viewer. Edit them live — straight from the pause menu, no relog, no file uploads.[/b]

Your rules and guides stop being a Discord link nobody opens and become a first-class, in-game window with a side menu and formatted text. Content lives in one folder on the server and is [b]streamed live[/b] to players: edit it and everyone sees the new version the next time they open the window. Built for dedicated / multiplayer servers — the client never touches the disk, it only receives text over the network.

[hr][/hr]
[h2]What it does[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]In-game guide & rules viewer[/b] — a window with a category menu on the left and formatted, scrollable text on the right.
[*][b]Live content[/b] — the guides live in a folder on the server; change them and players get the new version on reopen. No client downloads, no relog.
[*][b]Read-only for players[/b] — they open, read and close. No "I have read and agree" gate, no blocking.
[*][b]Opens on join[/b] — the window pops up automatically every time a player enters the server, so newcomers actually see your rules. Each player can switch this off with a checkbox in the window.
[*][b]Set the landing page[/b] — choose which page opens by default (e.g. your top rule or a welcome page). Without it, the guide opens the first page.
[*][b]Collapsible categories[/b] — click a category in the side menu to expand or collapse its pages, so long menus stay tidy.
[*][b]Opens from the pause menu[/b] — a [b]Server Guide[/b] entry in the pause menu (Esc) opens it anytime.
[/list]

[hr][/hr]
[h2]Edit in-game (staff only)[/h2]
Your staff never has to FTP into the server to fix a typo. Open the guide window and you get two extra buttons:
[list]
[*][b]Edit[/b] — edit the current page's text right there (the raw rich-text markup). Save, and the change is written on the server and goes live for everyone.
[*][b]Edit menu[/b] — create / rename / remove categories and pages, mark a category as [i]Rules[/i], reorder, and pick the default [i]home[/i] page ([i]Set as home[/i]) — all from the UI. New pages get their file created automatically.
[/list]
[b]Who can edit is up to you[/b] — a sandbox option lists the access levels allowed (default [i]admin;moderator;overseer;gm[/i]; leave empty to allow none). The single-player / co-op host can always edit.

[hr][/hr]
[h2]Multiplayer-ready[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Server-authoritative[/b] — only the server reads and writes the files. Every edit is re-validated on the server (access level, safe path, 256 KB limit); the buttons are cosmetic, a client can't forge a write.
[*][b]Streamed safely[/b] — pages are sliced into chunks over the network and reassembled on the client, so large guides just work.
[*][b]Live sync[/b] — saved edits broadcast to everyone; no relog.
[/list]

[hr][/hr]
[h2]Formatting & images[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Rich text[/b] — write your pages with the native [i]ISRichTextPanel[/i] tags (see the list below).
[*][b]Images[/b] — reference an image packed in a loaded mod's [i]media/[/i] folder by name. A demo image and a separate example image-mod are included so you can ship your own.
[/list]

[b]Supported tags:[/b]
[list]
[*][b]<LINE>[/b] — line break
[*][b]<SIZE:small|medium|large>[/b] — font size
[*][b]<RGB:r,g,b>[/b] — text color (values 0–1)
[*][b]<PUSHRGB:r,g,b>[/b] / [b]<POPRGB>[/b] — push/pop a color (for inline colored spans)
[*][b]<RED> <GREEN> <ORANGE>[/b] — quick colors
[*][b]<CENTRE> <LEFT> <RIGHT>[/b] — text alignment
[*][b]<INDENT:n>[/b] / [b]<SETX:n>[/b] — indent / set X position (pixels)
[*][b]<SPACE>[/b] — a space
[*][b]<IMAGE:name>[/b] / [b]<IMAGECENTRE:name,width,height>[/b] — show an image (by media/ name)
[/list]

[b]Spacing around inline colors[/b] — the rich-text panel has two quirks to know when coloring a word mid-sentence:
[list]
[*][b]Put a space before a closing tag[/b] — text glued directly before a tag is dropped, so write [b]word <POPRGB>[/b], never [b]word<POPRGB>[/b] (otherwise "word" disappears).
[*][b]Use <SPACE> next to a color change[/b] — a normal space beside a color tag isn't rendered (words end up glued, e.g. "opcaoGerar"). Insert [b]<SPACE>[/b] to force the gap. Pattern: [b]before <SPACE><PUSHRGB:1,0.82,0.3>colored <POPRGB><SPACE>after[/b] (skip the trailing <SPACE> if punctuation like ":" follows).
[/list]

[hr][/hr]
[h2]Using images[/h2]
The text is streamed live, but [b]images are not[/b] — an image must be packed in a loaded mod's [i]media/[/i] folder (that's the only place the game scans into its texture map and syncs to clients). You then reference it [b]by name[/b], starting from [i]media/[/i] (the mod name is NOT part of the path):
[list]
[*]Put your PNGs in a mod under [i]media/ui/guias/[/i] (a unique subfolder avoids clashes with other mods).
[*]In a guide page, write [b]<IMAGECENTRE:media/ui/guias/yourimage.png,512,512>[/b] (or [b]<IMAGE:media/ui/guias/yourimage.png>[/b]).
[/list]
A demo image ships with this mod. To add [b]your own[/b] images without editing this mod, use the companion mod [b][url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3743487241]ServerGuide Images Example[/url][/b] as a template. In multiplayer that image mod must be on the Workshop (local mods don't sync to clients).

[b]Image size[/b] — there is no hard pixel limit (it's bounded by the GPU's max texture size, normally well above 4096px), but for performance:
[list]
[*]Use [b]power-of-two[/b] dimensions (256, 512, 1024…). The engine pads any other size up to the next power of two in video memory, so a 513px image costs as much as 1024px.
[*]The image is scaled to the [b]width,height in <IMAGECENTRE:…,w,h>[/b] — don't ship a file much larger than you actually display.
[*]Keep dimensions at/under ~2048px to be safe on older GPUs, and keep the file small: every client downloads the image mod.
[/list]

[hr][/hr]
[h2]Setup[/h2]
[olist]
[*]Enable the mod on the server (and on clients in MP, via the Workshop).
[*]On first run it creates [i]~/Zomboid/Lua/ServerGuide/[/i] and fills it with template files — it never overwrites existing content.
[*]Edit the guides in-game with the [b]Edit[/b] / [b]Edit menu[/b] buttons (staff), or edit the [i].txt[/i] files directly on the server (UTF-8).
[*]Players open the window from the [b]Server Guide[/b] button in the pause menu (Esc) — and it opens automatically on join.
[/olist]

[hr][/hr]
[h2]Sandbox options[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Access levels allowed to edit[/b] — a semicolon-separated list of roles that may edit in-game (default [i]admin;moderator;overseer;gm[/i]).
[/list]

[hr][/hr]
[h2]Languages[/h2]
English and Português (Brasil).

[hr][/hr]
[i]Build 42. Safe to add to an existing server: it only creates its folder if missing and never overwrites your content.[/i]

[hr][/hr]
